        "question_title": "If \\( \\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{7-x}=4 \\) has real solutions \\(x_1\\) and \\(x_2\\), find \\(x_1+x_2\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Squaring gives \\(10+2\\sqrt{(x+3)(7-x)}=16\\), so \\((x+3)(7-x)=9\\). Hence \\(x^2-4x-12=0\\), giving \\(x=-2,6\\). Therefore, \\(x_1+x_2=4\\).",
